---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How FCMOBILETOOLS collects, uses and protects information when you use the website.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: October 9, 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Information you provide</h2>
      <p>You can read public pages and use most calculators without registering. If you create an account, we may collect your email address, username, display name, avatar and any profile details you choose to provide.</p>
      <p>If you use account features, we may also keep records of your quests and progress, XP and Token balances, survey answers, community votes, achievements, leaderboard results, reward activity and tournament participation. If you contact us or submit content, we use the information and material you send to respond, review it or publish it where appropriate.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. Information collected when you visit</h2>
      <p>When you visit the site, basic technical information may be processed to load pages, keep the site secure and understand how it is used. This may include your IP address, browser or device information, pages visited, referring page and request times. Cookies and similar technologies may also be used as described in our <a href="/legal/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
      <p>We use information to provide the site and its features, maintain accounts, show your chosen profile details, track eligible progress, administer surveys and rewards, display community results, respond to requests, fix problems, prevent abuse and improve our content.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. What other visitors can see</h2>
      <p>Some information may appear publicly when you use a public profile, leaderboard, community vote or tournament feature. Depending on the feature and your choices, this may include your username, avatar, public profile details, ranking or competition information. Survey answers and account contact details are not published as public profile information. Avoid placing private or sensitive information in public fields or submissions.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>We use Google Analytics to understand site traffic and how pages are used. The site may also display advertisements provided by Google. When Google services run on a page, your browser may send information such as the page address, IP address, browser details and identifiers. Google and its advertising partners may use cookies, web beacons or similar technologies to deliver ads, measure performance, prevent repeated ads or personalise advertising according to your settings and applicable consent choices.</p>
      <p>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a> and manage ad personalisation through <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. When information is shared</h2>
      <p>We may share limited information with service providers that help us run the site, provide account sign-in, host media, measure usage, serve advertisements or protect against abuse. They may process information as needed to provide those services and under their own terms and privacy policies.</p>
      <p>We may also disclose information when reasonably necessary to respond to a lawful request, protect users, address fraud or misuse, or protect our rights and the security of the site. We do not publish your account email address or sell your survey answers as public content.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Storage and retention</h2>
      <p>Some preferences or tool progress may be saved in your browser. Account activity and submissions may be retained for as long as needed to provide the relevant feature, maintain accurate records, address misuse or disputes, or meet legal obligations. Retention periods can vary by information type and purpose.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
      <p>You can manage cookies through your browser and use the <strong>Privacy Choices</strong> link in the site footer where available. You can also contact us to request access to, correction of or deletion of personal information you provided. We may need to verify your request, and some information may need to be retained for legitimate security, accounting or legal reasons. Your rights depend on the laws that apply to you.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Children</h2>
      <p>Please do not submit another person's personal information without permission. If you are a parent or guardian and believe a child has provided personal information to the site, contact us through the <a href="/legal/contact">Contact page</a> so we can review the concern.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy when the site or its services change. The date at the top shows when it was last revised. For privacy questions or requests, use the official channels on our <a href="/legal/contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
